      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE GOLDEN HOOK (7) settled close to the pace then assumed control and kept finding to return to the winners' list last start over 2190m at this track, getting there by 3 metres. May need luck at some stage extracting from the inside of the second row. Won't find this any harder and he can add to his recent outstanding results. FOXY TWO GLOVES (4) is a talented mare first up from a break of seven months who generally comes to hand quickly. Scored a fine win over 1790m at this track to launch her last preparation. Will be ready to run a big race. MIDNIGHT PIRATE (5) should be at his peak for this. Finished second over 2190m at this track at the latest appearance two weeks ago. Sure to give the top fancies plenty to think about. LISTEN TO THE HAND (3) is worth some thought based on his victory over 1609m at Gawler two runs ago.",
